\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a) Representation-consistent reconstruction: exact inversion precedes intensity residual compensation and clipping. (b) Masked post-adaptation (AMS): the entire model, including the compensator, receives $Y_m$, which replaces the generic input $Y$ in (a); unmasked $Y$ supplies the noisy target. Only the Transformer encoder is frozen. Training masks are resampled; fixed validation masks support checkpoint selection. Inference uses unmasked observations.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:representation_ams}{{3}{4}}
